{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1497613-cold-iron-cog-soldiers-in-c-td-and-in-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt","id":1497613,"title":"Cold iron cog-soldiers in C:tD and in Arcadia: the Wyld Hunt?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-20T00:27:26-08:00","id":1497613,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Cold iron cog-soldiers in C:tD and in Arcadia: the Wyld Hunt?","content":"In Dreams &amp; Nightmares, and also in Arcadia: the Wyld Hunt and King Ironheart's Madness, we were introduced to the concept of chimerical cold iron, i.e. cold iron which could be found in the Dreaming (and not brought into it, as per the terrible experience of the Dauntain at Versailles). <br /> <br /> <br /> How do you think this cold iron would work, rule-wise? <br /> <br /> <br /> More difficult question: what does it say about the nature of the Dreaming, of Glamour, of Banality and the relationship of cold iron to all these things?<br /> <br /> A related question: <br /> We all remember fondly Arcadia: the Wyld Hunt and its sequel, King's Ironheart Madness.I remember how I was fascinated by the ads that were published juste before KAM release, like the one at the back of the Shadow Court sourcebook or others (the top part was always identical while the bottom part changed according to the character. I know three of them: dragonkin warrior, imp adventurer and redcap brute).<br /> <br /> <br /> Now in the text, we can read: <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;He commands a legion of soulless cold-iron warriors that no army of the fae can withstand.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But when the game actually came out, it didn't seem that the cog soldiers were not made out of cold-iron, except for the information on just one card in King Ironheart's Madness, Kelwrath's Volcano:<br /> \u201cKelwrath\u2019s Volcano is the secret source of the Cold Iron used to bring the Cog Armies of Middlemarch to life.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> It's indicated in the card text that Cog or Mechorgs who Rest in this League can recover 3 Abilities or Treasures.<br /> <br /> <br /> This means, that, indeed, the Cog soldiers and Mechorgs are made out of Cold Iron.<br /> <br /> <br /> How can this be? What does it tell us about the nature of Cold Iron, its relationship with Banality, with Glamour, with the Fomorian Dream (as I'm sure that King Ironheart's &quot;Madness&quot; is one born out of Nightmare and the Fomorian Dream, much like Bedlam is in C20).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T19:23:41-07:00","id":1507531,"title":"","content":"I included two paragraphs about this in &quot;Lords of Nightmare&quot; and would like to develop it more in the finished product.<br /> <br /> Would you like to share information?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T03:29:47-07:00","id":1509159,"title":"","content":"This is just a guess, but because it is cold iron created in the dream, it may have different characteristics from the original cold iron, perhaps this is just a weapon resistant to faerie powers, since if it were done differently, nockers could easily dismantle it or make something capable of rivaling, Redcaps could simply rip parts of them off with their teeth and even use chimeras against, apart from that they can possibly be resistant against banality, I imagine these changes were to not make them almost unbeatable. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}